      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Workers of Far East Railway were diagnosed as having various disorders of free-radical oxidation processes due to occupational factors. Oxidative stress parameters were changed even at preclinical stages of broncho-pulmonary diseases--that evidence could be useful for early diagnosis of pulmonary diseases in individuals exposed to hazards."},
